<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-season7" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Season 7: Operations with Variables</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> 
        In Season 01, we learned how to add, subtract, multiply, divide, and do exponents with whole numbers.
      </p>
      <p>
        In Season 02, we learned how to add, subtract, multiply, divide, and do exponents with negative numbers.
      </p>
      <p>
       In Season 03, we learned how to add, subtract, multiply, divide, and do exponents with fractions.
      </p>
      <p>
        In Season 04, we learned how to add, subtract, multiply, divide, and do exponents with decimals.
      </p>
      <p>
        In this season, we’re going to learn how to add, subtract, multiply, divide, and do exponents with variables, which represent numbers that are changing or unknown. 
        Because a variable can theoretically have any value, 
        when we’re doing operations with variables, we need to make sure that the steps we’re taking are valid for all values.
      </p>
  </introduction>
